      "description": "Watch Italy vs Belgium highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 25, 2026. A Tactical Battle in the UEFA Nations League On September 25, 2026, Italy hosted Belgium in a high-stakes UEFA Nations League fixture that drew a crowd of 47,155 spectators. Both sides approached the match with caution, fighting for control in the midfield as they looked to break the deadlock in a competitive atmosphere. Belgium Seizes the Advantage Belgium proved to be the more clinical side, capitalising on a defensive slip-up by the hosts in the 20th minute. Kevin De Bruyne provided the decisive assist for Mika Godts , who coolly found the back of the net with his right foot. While Italy responded with renewed energy, repeatedly testing goalkeeper Senne Lammens through headers from Francesco Pio Esposito and Gianluca Mancini , the Belgium defense held firm to maintain their lead into the interval. Second Half Drama and Discipline As the game progressed into the second half, Dodi Lukebakio delivered a stunning strike from outside the box in the 69th minute to double the lead. The closing stages saw the intensity boil over, resulting in a flurry of yellow cards for dissent and tactical fouls. Despite a late opportunity for Giorgio Scalvini , who narrowly missed the target, Italy could not find a way back, leaving Belgium to secure a hard-fought victory."
